<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells 280 trln lira of 11-mth bills.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells 280 trln lira of 11-mth bills.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish Treasury met half of the bids in an auction on Tuesday by selling 280 trln lira of 11-month bills at a lower yield, after last Tuesday's auction where it sold 229.1 trillion lira of 10-month bills at 125.08 percent yield (including witholding tax).</p>
<p>Results on page  CBTI.</p>
<p>    Amount	: 280 trillion lira</p>
<p>Total bids  : 564.79 trillion lira</p>
<p>    Max yield   : 120.37 percent (including witholding tax)</p>
<p>    Maturity    : June 10, 1998</p>
<p>Value date  : July 16, 1997</p>
<p>Banks will pay 134.3 trillion lira to the Treasury for the auction on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75 EKS</p>
</text>
